Attribute VB_Name = "netplay_c"
' lib/netplay/netplay.cpp, lib/netplay/netplay.h (1 of 4): the state (NETPLAY NetPlay with its PLAYERs,
' the sockets, the temporary join sockets' states, the statistics, the game details the lobby listing
' would carry), the settings, the version, the password and lock, the player slots (NET_InitPlayer(s),
' NET_CreatePlayer, NET_DestroyPlayer, the open-slot searches), the players' info messages, the names,
' the game flags, NETinit, NETshutdown, netplayShutDown, the statistics, the connection status icons and
' messageTypeToString. netplay_conn_c has the connections (send, receive, host, join), netplay_sys_c the
' system messages and the player index swaps, netplay_file_c the file transfers.
' The game's side (multiplay.cpp's game and ingame, multijoin, multistat, ...) is reached through
' INetGame (netGame). Port mapping is port_mapping_manager_c's (libplum), the lobby server's hosting handler
' the exe's (netlobby_c here forwards to it through INetGame; cluster J part 2). The ActivityManager (the
' activity sinks) is not ported: its calls are comments.
' std::set<uint32_t> of player indexes are Boolean arrays walked in ascending order; std::chrono's
' steady_clock is steadyNowMs (milliseconds, a Double).
Option Explicit

